# maluos-apple-t2: what an Intel Mac with the T2 chip (2018 on) needs beyond
# Ubuntu 26.04's kernel, which already carries the Touch Bar (appletbdrm,
# hid-appletb-kbd/bl), apple-gmux for the T2, the CS8409 codec and brcmfmac.
# The installer adds this component on a T2 Mac (docs/phase11-apple-t2.md);
# the live medium carries the driver parts (image/profiles/live.pkgs). The
# PipeWire DSP t2-dsp stays in the repository, off the medium: it would pull
# PipeWire and the LV2 plugins (150 MB) onto every medium for a desktop nicety.
maluos-apple-t2-support
apple-bce-dkms
applesmc-t2
bcm5974-t2
apple-t2-audio-config
dkms
linux-headers-generic
mesa-vulkan-drivers
libvulkan1
?tiny-dfr
?t2fanrd
?apple-firmware-script
?apfs-dkms
?vulkan-tools
